@1 = ~Trademeet Haunting~
@2 = ~A restless spectre in Trademeet asked us to find her missing child. She claims a wicked man named Hodrig, west of the cemetery, took him. The spirit cannot rest until the child is returned.~
@3 = ~We recovered the child's body from Hodrig and returned it to the spectre. Reunited with what remained of her child, the spirit was finally able to find peace.~

// New English dialogue strings extracted for localisation.
@4 = ~I never trusted Djinis. Those shady, shifty eyes hide so many secrets.~
@5 = ~Djinis, animals, adventurers. How more crowded will this city become?~
@6 = ~Some folk claim they can see a ghost at the cemetery at night. Who would believe that nonsense.~
@7 = ~When I was younger I dreamed about being like you. Intrepid traveller who seeks adventures and wealth. But rotten tombs and catacombs are officially not my thing.~
@8 = ~Some way to shatter one's dream, Mazzy.~
@9 = ~My children keep telling stories about a ghost manifesting after nightfall. This is truly a wonder.~
@10 = ~Actually, they are teenagers. I should sit down and speak to them properly.~
@11 = ~Usually locals pick on me cause I am a Tiefling, but since you're here, take some of that attention. The less harassment I get, the better.~
@12 = ~I hope you're here to help, not cause trouble.~
@13 = ~Had Waukeen be alive she'd never allow this to happen. Dao taking over our town's trade? Animals and filthy druids trying to make this place their home? What's next?~
@14 = ~Phi. I've met enough druids to know what you're all like. Vicious savages.~
@15 = ~I'll focus it on whoever I want.~
@16 = ~I came all this way from the City of Coin to set up my business here, only to be met with ruin! Bandits plundered my merchandise, slaughtered my horse, and to top it all off, I couldn't open my shop here even if I begged! This is an absolute calamity.~
@17 = ~Did you... take my child...?~
@18 = ~Evan... where is he... my child... they took him... I won't rest until I find him...~
@19 = ~Hodrig... west of here. Evil man... wicked.~
@20 = ~Please... get him back... west...~
@21 = ~Please... get him back... west...~
@22 = ~My child... she...~
@23 = ~My child...~
@24 = ~My child...~
@25 = ~Find him... west...~
@26 = ~Marcos!... reunited finally...~
@27 = ~What do you want, fools?! Why are you bothering me!~
@28 = ~Who? Reeva's? Haha! Ain't that something. You came to play a hero, yeah? Let me teach you some manners. Kill them all!~
@29 = ~Wait, wait! Stop! I yield! Just... don't kill me! Here! You can have this kid!~
@30 = ~Okay! I promise I won't do so again! I will quit this job. Darsidian doesn't even pay me enough.~
@31 = ~How barbaric! You won't spare a man who concede?! So be it!~
@32 = ~If you need anything, darling, talk to Vyatri. I'm just a cook here.~
@33 = ~No trouble out of you. Have a hot meal, but keep your weapons sheathed.~
@34 = ~Our way of life is full of perils. I assure you, Cindrax, you wouldn't like that. I know your heart and how delicate it is.~
@35 = ~They are children. Of course, their imagination runs wild.~
@36 = ~You'll have no trouble from us. I promise.~
@37 = ~I perfectly understand your frustration but not all druids are to blame for his misconduct.~
@38 = ~You're clouded by rigid preconceptions. The true servant of the Oak is not a force of destruction, but a keeper of the Great Cycle, striving ever for the prosperity of the verdant wilds. It is the Shadow Druids who have disrupted the balance. It is upon them that your anger should focus on.~
@39 = ~Your sensitivity is exasperating, kobold. Stop desponding, start working harder.~
@40 = ~(sigh) If we must continue to squander precious moments on this triviality, know this: certain pathetic spirits remain tethered to this wretched mortal realm, bound tightly to some object or a person. Until their unfinished business is settled, their souls cannot pass into the void beyond. They are trapped by their own design.~
@41 = ~If we must tarry for this, listen. Some spirits remain tethered to the living world, bound to a specific trinket or a mortal soul. Their essence cannot cross into the quiet dark until their lingering tasks are fulfilled. Let us see it done quickly, then; my patience is not infinite.~

// CotSC localisation batch 4: player-visible text extracted; original entries unchanged.
@42 = ~W-what?~
@43 = ~No, I have not.~
@44 = ~I have to go.~
@45 = ~Who took your child?~
@46 = ~This isn't my business. I am leaving.~
@47 = ~Hold on. We will get your child back.~
@48 = ~Viconia? Anything?~
@49 = ~Hexxat? What is it?~
@50 = ~I don't have time for this.~
@51 = ~I'm still searching.~
@52 = ~We found your child. Hodrig paid for what he did.~
@53 = ~I'm still searching.~
@54 = ~I know you took the child of a young woman from the area. Where is he?~
@55 = ~Nothing in particular.~
@56 = ~Fine, fine. I'm leaving.~
@57 = ~His... body? You killed him?! Get out of here before I change my mind!~
@58 = ~His... body? You killed him?! I won't let that slide! Die!~
